WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Imagine an ai that plans your whole trip and books it for you like a super organized friend. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 219. After the travel news, how these helpers actually choose their next move, a video chat avatar you can talk to, and a ring that speaks without a phone. Airbnb is building its own artificial intelligence or ai travel agent. The Verge reported from the company's third quarter, 2026 shareholder letter. An agent here means a helper that can take many

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.592
steps in a row. Not just answer one question and stop. The tool is set to launch in the

00:00:35.592 --> 00:00:41.372
first half of 2027, and it will help people plan trips, compare homes, manage bookings,

00:00:41.692 --> 00:00:46.932
and get help during a stay. Picture a travel buddy who already knows what you like, and can

00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:52.272
pull up maps, photos, and itineraries without you typing a long list of questions. Instead

00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:57.272
of a regular chat that only answers in text, this agent builds a custom screen with the

00:00:57.272 --> 00:01:01.972
right visuals at the right moment, almost like a mini travel app that appears instantly.

00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:08.352
Airbnb CEO Brian Cheskey explained that today's AI agents handle simple tasks such as making

00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:11.252
a restaurant reservation or scheduling an appointment.

00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:16.592
Planning a trip works differently, he said, because it is aspirational, which just means

00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:20.032
you are dreaming and browsing, not ticking off one tiny to do.

00:01:20.572 --> 00:01:25.432
The company noted that 80% of travelers say they enjoy spending time researching trips,

00:01:25.432 --> 00:01:28.332
and people want to look at photos, compare homes,

00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:31.752
and make decisions with the friends or family they are traveling with.

00:01:32.172 --> 00:01:34.672
Think of it like a group chat for a weekend hangout.

00:01:35.172 --> 00:01:37.012
Nobody wants a giant wall of text.

00:01:37.432 --> 00:01:40.852
You want the photos, the map pin, and the calendar sitting there

00:01:40.852 --> 00:01:42.472
so everyone can weigh in together.

00:01:43.092 --> 00:01:46.552
The new agent draws from a library of hundreds of travel-specific

00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:50.332
interface components, including maps, photos, comparisons,

00:01:51.032 --> 00:01:52.492
calendars, and itineraries.

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:56.392
then composes them in real-time to match what the user is looking for.

00:01:57.032 --> 00:02:01.632
Interface components are just the building blocks of a screen, like Lego pieces for maps

00:02:01.632 --> 00:02:04.452
and photo grids, snapped together while you talk.

00:02:05.052 --> 00:02:10.252
That matters because general-purpose chatbots are text-heavy, while travel benefits from visual

00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:12.092
browsing and shared decision-making.

00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:16.412
A chatbot is simply a program you type to, and it types back.

00:02:16.792 --> 00:02:20.772
Find for a quick fact, awkward when you are trying to fall in love with a place.

00:02:20.772 --> 00:02:26.352
For a teen planning a school break or a family vacation, it could mean fewer tabs open

00:02:26.352 --> 00:02:28.752
and more time actually looking at cool places.

00:02:29.172 --> 00:02:33.672
The company says it is making the agent because it's experience matching hosts and guests.

00:02:34.192 --> 00:02:38.872
Plus its role in existing reservations gives it an edge over other AI tools.

00:02:39.372 --> 00:02:43.952
The announcement also described the agent as having a personalized interface built specifically

00:02:43.952 --> 00:02:48.572
for travel, offering the right interface at the right time based on what guests are

00:02:48.572 --> 00:02:49.172
looking for.

00:02:49.172 --> 00:02:54.432
You cannot try it yet, but you can follow Airbnb's updates on their site or app to see

00:02:54.432 --> 00:02:55.972
early previews when they appear.

00:02:56.942 --> 00:03:01.122
You know how when you are texting about weekend plans, your phone sometimes guesses the

00:03:01.122 --> 00:03:04.922
next word or suggests a whole reply based on what you just said?

00:03:05.442 --> 00:03:07.782
Stretch that same idea across many steps.

00:03:08.382 --> 00:03:10.422
The AI does not just guess one word.

00:03:10.922 --> 00:03:15.642
It keeps track of your whole conversation and decides what task to do next, like pulling

00:03:15.642 --> 00:03:19.022
up a map or suggesting three places that match what you described.

00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:25.242
It can also remember earlier details you mentioned, such as I like quiet spots, and use that

00:03:25.242 --> 00:03:27.262
memory later without you repeating yourself.

00:03:27.862 --> 00:03:32.462
That memory is less like a locker where a fax sits forever, and more like a sticky note

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:35.362
that helps or carries from room to room as the plan changes.

00:03:36.002 --> 00:03:41.402
The system works by breaking big goals into smaller actions it can handle one at a time, checking

00:03:41.402 --> 00:03:44.682
what it already knows and what it still needs to ask or look up.

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:47.762
It is the same move you use on a big school project.

00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:50.262
You do not write the whole essay in one breath.

00:03:50.742 --> 00:03:54.602
You pick a topic, then find three sources, then outline, then write.

00:03:55.162 --> 00:03:56.942
Checking what you still need at each step.

00:03:57.422 --> 00:04:01.962
Over time it gets better at choosing the right action because it has seen thousands of similar

00:04:01.962 --> 00:04:03.122
conversations before.

00:04:03.722 --> 00:04:07.302
The way you get faster at packing once you have packed for camp a few times.

00:04:07.942 --> 00:04:12.702
Open your messages right now, start a text about weekend plans, and watch how your phone

00:04:12.702 --> 00:04:18.762
suggests the next word or a whole reply. That tiny guess is the seed. An agent is that seed,

00:04:19.042 --> 00:04:23.962
grown up, choosing the next job instead of the next word. Once you have watched those suggestions

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:29.702
pop up, you already understand the basic loop. Track the chat, pick a next action, check what

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:35.555
is missing, repeat until the plan is done. A customizable animated character called Muse

00:04:35.555 --> 00:04:41.655
can now hold a real-time video conversation with you, after Meta opened the feature in its AI app.

00:04:41.655 --> 00:04:47.195
The avatar can show expressions and respond with voice, making the chat feel more like talking

00:04:47.195 --> 00:04:48.875
to someone than typing at a screen.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:54.575
It is fun if you like creative roleplay or just want a more natural way to practice conversations,

00:04:54.975 --> 00:04:57.915
because the face on screen actually reacts while you speak.

00:04:58.415 --> 00:05:03.175
The feature rolled out first to a verge writer on the iPhone app, where the avatar appears

00:05:03.175 --> 00:05:04.935
at the top of the screen during the call.

00:05:05.435 --> 00:05:10.515
You can try it right now in the meta AI app on iOS, which is Apple's iPhone software

00:05:10.515 --> 00:05:15.215
by starting a voice chat and choosing the Avatar option, ask it to act like a

00:05:15.215 --> 00:05:19.775
character from your favorite show or help you brainstorm a story idea and watch

00:05:19.775 --> 00:05:23.895
its reactions on screen while it talks. The expressive avatar makes the

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:27.695
interaction feel more alive because it reacts in real time to what you say,

00:05:28.135 --> 00:05:33.606
closer to a video called in a comment box. 11 labs in SoundCloud teamed up so

00:05:33.606 --> 00:05:37.566
you can create music with AI and post it directly to the platform without

00:05:37.566 --> 00:05:42.306
downloading files first. SoundCloud artist pro subscribers even get three months

00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:47.166
of free 11 labs access as part of the deal. This is exciting if you make beats or

00:05:47.166 --> 00:05:51.406
songs for fun and want to share them quickly, because the extra step of exporting

00:05:51.406 --> 00:05:55.686
audio and uploading it separately is gone. Think of it like posting a story

00:05:55.686 --> 00:06:00.946
without saving the photo to your camera roll first. Make it, send it done. Go to

00:06:00.946 --> 00:06:05.726
the 11 Labs website or app, generate a short track, and look for the new SoundCloud

00:06:05.726 --> 00:06:10.586
published button to test it out. Once published, the track appears on your soundcloud profile

00:06:10.586 --> 00:06:17.214
right away, ready for others to hear. Aina's new ring, TechCrunch reported, has a tiny screen,

00:06:17.574 --> 00:06:23.094
a joystick, and a microphone so you can speak to AI helpers, take calls, or dictate notes without

00:06:23.094 --> 00:06:28.154
pulling out your phone. It is designed to feel like a wearable remote control for AI tools you

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:33.934
already use. A tiny clicker on your finger instead of another slab in your pocket. The ring also

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:39.234
works for dictating notes directly on a Mac, giving a hands-free way to interact with AI agents

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:44.674
on the go. That's it for today. Remember, every AI expert started exactly where you are right

00:06:44.674 --> 00:06:49.894
now. If something we talked about today made you curious, go try it. That's literally how

00:06:49.894 --> 00:06:55.434
learning works. Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we'll see you tomorrow. And if you'd rather

